# Security Review Quick Reference

## 🚨 Critical Issues (Fix Now!)

### 1. No Authentication
```javascript
// ❌ VULNERABLE
app.get('/users', (req, res) => res.json(users));

// ✅ SECURE
app.get('/users', authenticateToken, (req, res) => res.json(users));
```

### 2. No Input Validation
```javascript
// ❌ VULNERABLE
app.get('/search', (req, res) => db.find({ name: req.query.q }));

// ✅ SECURE
app.get('/search', validateQueryParams, (req, res) => {
  if (!validator.isAlphanumeric(req.query.q)) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid query' });
  }
  db.find({ name: req.query.q });
});
```

### 3. No Rate Limiting
```javascript
// ❌ VULNERABLE
app.get('/users', (req, res) => res.json(users));

// ✅ SECURE
const limiter = rateLimit({ max: 100, windowMs: 900000 });
app.use(limiter);
app.get('/users', (req, res) => res.json(users));
```

### 4. No Security Headers
```javascript
// ❌ VULNERABLE
const app = express();
app.get('/health', (req, res) => res.json({ ok: true }));

// ✅ SECURE
const helmet = require('helmet');
const app = express();
app.use(helmet());
app.get('/health', (req, res) => res.json({ ok: true }));
```

### 5. Exposed Sensitive Data
```javascript
// ❌ VULNERABLE
res.json([
  { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com', password: 'hashed...' },
  { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com', password: 'hashed...' }
]);

// ✅ SECURE
