VULNERABILITY #4: MISSING SECURITY HEADERS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Location: Server configuration
Severity: HIGH

Current Code:
  // No security headers configured!

Attack Vectors:
  - Clickjacking: Attacker frames site in malicious context
  - XSS: Scripts from any origin execute
  - MIME sniffing: Browser interprets content as different type
  - Unencrypted traffic: HTTP not redirected to HTTPS

Headers Needed:

  X-Frame-Options: DENY
    → Prevents clickjacking

  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
    → Prevents MIME sniffing

  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'
    → Prevents inline scripts and XSS

  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
    → Forces HTTPS

  X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block
    → Browser XSS protection

Remediation:

  const helmet = require('helmet');

  app.use(helmet());

  // Or configure individually:
  app.use(helmet.frameguard({ action: 'deny' }));
  app.use(helmet.noSniff());
  app.use(helmet.contentSecurityPolicy({
    directives: {
      defaultSrc: ["'self'"],
      scriptSrc: ["'self'"],
    }
  }));
  app.use(helmet.hsts({
    maxAge: 31536000,
    includeSubDomains: true,
    preload: true
  }));

