## A05:2021 – Broken Access Control

### Description
The application fails to enforce restrictions on what authenticated users can do. This includes:
- Missing object-level authorization checks
- Broken function-level access control
- Insecure direct object references (IDOR)

### Vulnerabilities in app.js

#### 1. **No Authorization Checks on Protected Data**
```javascript
// VULNERABLE
app.get('/users/:id', authenticate, (req, res) => {
  const userId = req.params.id;
  // No check if user is accessing their own data
  return res.json(getUserData(userId));
});

// User 1 could access User 2's data!
// GET /users/2 (as user 1)
```

**Fix:**
```javascript
app.get('/api/users/:id', authenticate, (req, res) => {
  const userId = parseInt(req.params.id);

  // Authorization check
  if (userId !== req.user.id && req.user.role !== 'admin') {
    return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Access denied' });
  }

  // Safe to return data
  res.json(getUserData(userId));
});
```

#### 2. **Mass Assignment Vulnerability**
```javascript
// VULNERABLE
app.post('/api/users', authenticate, (req, res) => {
  // User could send: { name: "Eve", role: "admin", isAdmin: true }
  const user = new User(req.body); // All fields accepted!
  user.save();
});
```

**Fix:**
```javascript
app.post('/api/users', authenticate, (req, res) => {
  const allowedFields = ['name', 'email', 'password'];
  const userData = {};

  allowedFields.forEach(field => {
    if (req.body[field] !== undefined) {
      userData[field] = req.body[field];
    }
  });

  // role and isAdmin fields are now ignored
  const user = new User(userData);
  user.save();
});
```

