## BEST PRACTICES SUMMARY

✅ DO:
- Use a dedicated secrets manager (Secrets Manager, Vault, Key Vault)
- Rotate secrets regularly (minimum 90 days)
- Store different secrets per environment
- Use IAM roles/policies to control access
- Enable audit logging for all secret access
- Implement secret versioning
- Use short-lived credentials where possible
- Encrypt secrets in transit and at rest

❌ DON'T:
- Store secrets in .env files (development only)
- Commit secrets to version control
- Share credentials between environments
- Store database passwords in plain text
- Use the same credentials across services
- Log sensitive data
- Hardcode credentials in source code
- Use test/staging credentials in production

