  res.on('finish', () => {
    logger.info({
      method: req.method,
      path: req.path,
      status: res.statusCode,
      ip: req.ip
    });
  });
  next();
});
```

---

### 8. MEDIUM: Error Handling

**Fix:**

Add global error handler (last middleware):
```javascript
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  const isDevelopment = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development';

  logger.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack
  });

  const errorResponse = {
    error: 'Internal server error'
  };

  if (isDevelopment) {
    errorResponse.stack = err.stack;
  }

  res.status(err.status || 500).json(errorResponse);
});
```

---

## Migration Checklist

- [ ] Install all security packages
- [ ] Create .env file from .env.example
- [ ] Add .env to .gitignore
- [ ] Replace app.js with secure version
- [ ] Run `npm audit` - should show no critical issues
- [ ] Test authentication flow
- [ ] Verify security headers: `curl -I http://localhost:3000`
- [ ] Test rate limiting (make rapid requests)
- [ ] Test validation (invalid inputs should fail)
- [ ] Check logs are being created
- [ ] Run unit tests
- [ ] Deploy to staging environment
- [ ] Run security scan on staging
- [ ] Deploy to production

---

## Testing Your Security Fixes

### Test Authentication
```bash
# Should fail - no token
curl http://localhost:3000/users

# Should succeed - with token
TOKEN=$(curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/login -d "username=demo&password=password" | jq -r '.token')
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" http://localhost:3000/users
```

### Test Security Headers
```bash
curl -I http://localhost:3000/health
# Look for: X-Frame-Options, Content-Security-Policy, etc.
```

### Test Input Validation
```bash
# Should fail - invalid ID
curl http://localhost:3000/users/abc

# Should succeed - valid ID
curl http://localhost:3000/users/1
```

### Test Rate Limiting
```bash
# Make 101 requests quickly
for i in {1..101}; do curl http://localhost:3000/users; done
# After 100, should get rate limit response
```

### Run Security Audit
```bash
npm audit
npm run lint:security
npm test
```

---

## Continuous Security

### Weekly
```bash
npm audit
npm update
```

### Before Each Deploy
```bash
npm audit
npm run lint:security
npm test
npm run test:security
```

### Quarterly
- Full penetration test
- Security code review
- Dependency update review
- Log review and analysis

---

## Common Issues & Troubleshooting

### Issue: JWT_SECRET Not Set
**Solution:**
```bash
echo "JWT_SECRET=your-very-long-random-secret" >> .env
# Generate secure secret:
node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
```

### Issue: CORS Errors
**Solution:**
```javascript
// Check ALLOWED_ORIGINS in .env
// Ensure frontend domain is in the list
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000,https://yourfrontend.com
```

### Issue: Can't Connect to Database
**Solution:**
```bash
# Verify connection string in .env
# Test connection separately before startup
node -e "require('./db').connect()"
```

### Issue: Logs Growing Too Large
**Solution:**
```javascript
// Implement log rotation
const DailyRotateFile = require('winston-daily-rotate-file');
new DailyRotateFile({ filename: 'app-%DATE%.log' })
```

---

## Resources

- OWASP Top 10: https://owasp.org/Top10/
- Express Security Best Practices: https://expressjs.com/en/advanced/best-practice-security.html
- Helmet.js: https://helmetjs.github.io/
- JWT Best Practices: https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8949
- NIST Cybersecurity Framework: https://www.nist.gov/cyberframework

EOF
cat REMEDIATION_GUIDE.md

