};

cloudwatch.putMetricAlarm(params).promise();
```

INCIDENT RESPONSE: COMPROMISED SECRET
======================================

If a secret is compromised:

1. IMMEDIATE (0-5 minutes)
   ├─ Declare incident
   ├─ Start incident command
   ├─ Assemble response team
   └─ Begin communication

2. IMMEDIATE ACTIONS (5-15 minutes)
   ├─ Disable old secret in secrets manager
   ├─ Generate new secret
   ├─ Update secrets manager with new value
   ├─ Monitor for errors during transition
   └─ Start rotation process

3. CONTAINMENT (15-60 minutes)
   ├─ Review access logs to see what was accessed
   ├─ Check for unauthorized activities
   ├─ Check downstream systems using the secret
   ├─ Reset dependent services if needed
   └─ Document timeline

4. RECOVERY (1-24 hours)
   ├─ Full rotation of all affected secrets
   ├─ Verify new secrets work correctly
   ├─ Test all dependent services
   ├─ Run security scans
   └─ Clear old secret from any backups

5. POST-INCIDENT (24+ hours)
   ├─ Root cause analysis
   ├─ Update security procedures
   ├─ Staff training
   ├─ Update documentation
   ├─ Notify affected users if needed
   └─ Schedule follow-up review

